{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/360493-where-have-i-seen-this-rite-of-denial-before","id":360493,"title":"Where Have I Seen This Rite Of Denial Before?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-05T13:06:56-08:00","id":360493,"title":"Where Have I Seen This Rite Of Denial Before?","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Chain</span></b><br /> They say the bonds of blood are stronger than steel; blood runs thicker than water, and so on and so forth. The Sources say that a mouthful of blood used <i>just right</i> can build such a bond.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 wp and 2 thimbles of blood<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The swig of blood burns the Cainite's tongue; they take 1L and are stricken mute for the rest of the Scene (and their voice croaks for the rest of the night.)<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The blood tastes like iron on their tongue, but nothing else happens.<br /> <b>Success:</b> With a moment of focus, the Hunter transforms the blood, leaving it sweet on their tongue; they may hold the blood in their mouths for the rest of the scene, at which point they spit it out, useless and spent. At any point before that happens, they can either swallow or spit out the blood, both taking a Reflexive action. If they spit out the blood, anyone else that swallows it before the end of the scene develops the Swooning condition towards the Cainite; swallowing it extends this property to the Hunter's blood.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As a success, and the blood is so delicious that anyone else that swallows it takes a Beat and regains one Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T15:39:21-08:00","id":360655,"title":"","content":"I have no idea - but I'm not fond of any Rite that isn't directly focused on targeting vampires or combat. It goes against the monomaniacal fanaticism of the Heresy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T15:52:40-08:00","id":360660,"title":"","content":"The title of the thread was meant to be a joke related to the fact that this is essentially a boiled-down version of Vinculum. One idea I've been playing with is having one type of Vampire be Cainite Slashers, who get (as part of their Scourge Talent) the ability to learn Rites &quot;naturally&quot;, and to power them by bleeding - kinda slip some truth into the &quot;we stole these from Vampires idea.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I've never been a fan of the ultra-focus of the Heresy; I've always felt that while that kind of thing is fine for Compacts, a Conspiracy should outgrow that kind of thing. Sure, they can still be focused on one type of Supernatural, but I feel that <i>all other forms of Supernatural shouldn't be an out-of-context problem</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:39:05-08:00","id":361393,"title":"","content":"I try to avoid ever being strict about the divide between Compacts and Conspiracy becuase the definition is so annoyingly vague. I could quite easily argue that the Canites are actually a Compact.<br /> <br /> But basically, I like diversity. They're the only Monomanical Conspiracy, that means diversity. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:42:35-08:00","id":361395,"title":"","content":"Plus they have pretty good reason for it, their holy leader being a vampiric false messiah, then being trained by the minerva vampire hunters. Enslaving people in a rough imitation of the vinculum seems like it would really gain the Heresy's ire. Maybe some sort of exiled faction would do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-06-2015, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T11:28:38-08:00","id":361472,"title":"","content